      "problem": "What are the $xy$-coordinates of the point $A?$\n\n$A\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$- and $y$-axes.\n\n* The point is $4$ units to the *right* of the origin, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis. So, its $x$-coordinate is $4.$\n\n* The point is $3$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, its $y$-coordinate is $-3.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of our point are $(4,-3).$",
